# Crystalis

### Quickstart Rules

## What is Crystalis?

Crystalis is a cooperative fantasy card game where **your deck is your life.**

Every hero and every enemy is represented by their own deck of standard playing cards. Every card in that deck represents one hit point. As combat progresses your deck slowly shrinks until eventually someone can no longer draw a card...

...and they die.

Unlike most deck builders, running out of cards is not an inconvenience—it's your defeat.

Every suit has a purpose:

- **♣ Clubs** – Attack your enemies.
- **♠ Spades** – Block incoming attacks.
- **♥ Hearts** – Recover cards from your discard pile.
- **♦ Diamonds (Crystals)** – Powerful utility and class abilities.

Every hero has unique abilities fuelled by suits of cards, allowing completely different play styles despite sharing the same core rules.

---

# Setup

For your first game:

- Choose the **Warrior** hero.
- Choose the **Goblin Swarm** enemy.
- Shuffle both decks separately.
- Draw **5 cards** into the Warrior's hand.
- Reveal **3 Goblin cards** face-up.

The revealed Goblin cards are what the Goblins intend to do this round.

---

# Hero Stats

Every hero has three attributes.

## Attack

Whenever you play a **Club**, deal damage equal to your Attack stat.

Damage is dealt by discarding cards from the top of the target's deck.

If a hero has Attack **4**, every Club deals **4 damage**.

---

## Defence

Whenever you play a **Spade**, you prepare one **Block**.

The next time you are attacked, one prepared Block is consumed.

That Block reduces damage by your Defence stat.

Example:

A Warrior has Defence **3**.
A Goblin attacks for **5** damage.
The Warrior blocks **3**, taking only **2** damage.
One Block is then discarded.
Each Block only protects against **one attack**, even if some defence is unused.

---

## Spirit

Whenever you play a **Heart**, return cards from your discard pile to the bottom of your deck equal to your Spirit stat.

A hero with Spirit **2** returns two chosen cards.

Healing doesn't create new hit points—it simply recovers ones you've already lost.

---

## Diamonds

Diamonds are known as **Crystals**.

Every hero may spend a Diamond as an action to retrieve **one card of their choice** from their discard pile into their hand.

Most heroes also use Diamonds to power unique abilities.

---

# Playing a Round

Every round follows the same sequence.

### 1. Heroes act

Beginning with the player holding the Initiative token, each hero takes their turn.

During your turn you may play up to **three cards**.

You can freely mix attacks, defence, healing and abilities.

When your turn ends, draw **two cards**.

---

### 2. Enemies act

Enemies resolve their revealed cards one at a time.

A Club attacks.
A Heart heals.
A Spade prepares defence.
A Diamond usually powers that enemy's special ability.

Once all revealed cards have resolved they are discarded.

New cards are revealed ready for the next round.

---

### 3. Pass Initiative

After every hero and enemy has acted, pass the Initiative token clockwise.

A new round begins.

---

# Example Round

Our Warrior faces a Goblin Swarm.

The Goblins reveal:

- **5♣**
- **8♥**
- **4♦**

The Warrior begins with five cards in hand.

They decide to play:

- **2♠** — prepare a Block.
- **6♣** — pay for _Shield Bash_, interrupting the Goblin's Heart.
- **4♣** — perform a basic attack.

The Warrior's Attack is **4**, so the Goblins discard four cards from their deck.

The Warrior draws two new cards.

Now the Goblins act.

Their Heart has already been discarded, so only their Club and Diamond remain.

Unfortunately the Club is now adjacent to the Diamond, triggering the Goblin Swarm's special rule.

Instead of attacking once, the Goblins attack **four times**.

The Warrior blocks the first strike with their prepared Spade, but the remaining attacks land, stripping several cards from the Warrior's deck.

The next round begins with both sides weaker than before.

